FILE controller-records/V025-STAGES-6-8-CONTRACT-v1.2-AMENDMENT-2026-09-09.md
     1	# V025 stages 6–8 contract — v1.2 amendment (controller; sealed 2026-09-09 ≈ 02:15 UTC, before any successor training)
     2	
     3	v1 (sha ba867d0d…) and v1.1 (sha 1e56e8d7…) are preserved. This amendment applies the round-9D review (C3 algorithm family) and the round-9A review (claim wording and calibration). Seeds, panel, arms, margins and the learner contract are unchanged.
     4	
     5	1. **§B5 corrected — interaction labels are uncapped.** Ψ_A for a selected coalition costs |A| + 2 evaluations, so it is computed for every coalition regardless of size (v1.7 erratum item 3). Only the exact per-user Shapley attribution remains capped at |A| ≤ 4 and is reporting-only. C3 training rows therefore carry Ψ_A for the actual selected set, with `credit_split = NOT_COMPUTED_LARGE_SET` above the cap.
     6	2. **§C2 — feature sufficiency for the set-conditioned head.** The encoder's input must contain, for the changed-user set and its affected beams: proposed and incumbent associations by physical identity, background occupancy and activation before and after insertion, the shared-resource relations among the affected beams, and the **pairwise cross-gain terms among the affected beams** (not only a scalar interference summary — a summary can hide exactly the difference that flips a coupled fixed point). Acceptance test T2 is extended: the information-twin pair must be separable with the full context and provably ambiguous when the cross-gain block is removed.
     7	3. **§C4 / report schema — honest axes for a learned S3.** Over one catalogue that is exactly evaluated, S3 cannot exceed S0's maximum of the same score; therefore the only admissible learned claims are (i) better realised closed-loop pooled EE under model mismatch, (ii) equal decision quality at materially lower measured end-to-end computation, or (iii) a measured residual task (search allocation, evaluation-count reduction). The claim axis is named before training. A learned escape proposer over a wider neighbourhood is **not** part of this study; it may be proposed later with its own declaration and only if profiling shows evaluation is the bottleneck.
     8	4. **§D2 / §E — calibration must report the decision bound's own error rate.** Acceptance test T3 additionally reports the **one-sided** coverage of the bound actually used for the decision (not only the two-sided interval coverage), at 5 / 12 / 16 / 24 seeds and for the 3 %, 5 % and 10 % date-SD scenarios, each with its Monte-Carlo uncertainty. Every reported interval carries the disclosure fields listed in v1.7 erratum item 6.
     9	5. **Report schema — anti-pattern statistics (round 9D).** The terminal report must contain, per contrast: net collision-avoidance value with both components unclipped; the additive-reversal frequency and whether the coordinator prevents them; escape recall and harmful-acceptance rate stratified by coalition size; top-choice agreement between the learned and exact selectors; the full decision-latency distribution including feature construction, catalogue generation, physics-call count, timeout frequency and fallback-inclusive outcomes; and the four experiments of §C3 reported separately and never interchanged.
    10	6. **Certified comparator.** A budget-limited S_UNI is an operational comparator and is labelled as such; only a S_UNI with a completed-neighbourhood termination certificate supports the "beyond exhaustive unilateral improvement" claim (v1.6 §4). An offline certified reference may be used to diagnose available joint headroom provided its different computational status is stated.
    11	
    12	Seal: sha256 in the companion `.sha256` file.

FILE controller-records/V025-PHYSICS-SUCCESSOR-PRIORITY-DECLARATION-2026-09-08.md
     1	# V025 physics successor — priority declaration (controller, sealed before any successor outcome; 2026-09-08, server clock ≈ 13:50 UTC)
     2	
     3	## Owner's requirements (verbatim intent, 2026-09-08 ≈ 13:48 UTC)
     4	1. The off-axis / elevation angle must genuinely influence transmit power and energy efficiency.
     5	2. C1, C2 and C3 must each genuinely raise pooled EE; C3 is the current blocker.
     6	3. Both successor architectures are to be developed and tested in parallel; they are not in conflict.
     7	
     8	## Declaration
     9	- **Primary system model: architecture (a) `V025-ANGLE-TPC-TDM-ACM`** — memoryless angle-aware power control (per 30.08 s step, per simultaneous slot configuration: p_u = min(1.65 W, γ*·(N + Î_u)/ĥ_u), ĥ_u = G^T(θ_u)·L_u·G^R, γ* = the 8PSK 2/3 threshold of EN 302 307-1 Table 13 with the 1.7 dB margin and roll-off 0.20 correction, i.e. 7.528 dB nominal; equal-airtime TDM; coupled nominal powers solved from a history-independent initialisation with frozen tolerance and residual certification; no segment memory). Chosen because it is the only candidate that satisfies requirement 1 by construction. This choice is made **before** any successor outcome and is independent of C3's result.
    10	- **Declared reference model: architecture (b) `V025-FIXED-EIRP-ACM`** — fixed 1.65 W RF per active beam with ACM (astra round-3 §2). Reported in every table beside (a).
    11	- **Architectural sensitivity: (a′)** — same target with equal FDM sub-bands (per-user RF ceiling 1.65/n_b, beam RF = Σ p_u, sub-band-consistent noise/PSD/overlap).
    12	- **Priority order of the 18-cell physics-settings matrix (fixed now):** `a0 > b0 > a′0 > aS > bS > a′S > aH > bH > a′H > aSH > bSH > a′SH > aT > bT > a′T`; U cells (uncapped Shannon) are diagnostic only and ineligible as primary. Treatments per astra round 3 §4 (0 = 47-subinterval integration, standby 0, interruption off, ACM cap + margin; T = snapshot; S = standby f = 1/12; H = conditional 62/142 ms useful-time interruption; SH = both; U = uncapped).
    13	- **Everything else** follows astra round 3 §2 (items 1, 3, 5–31 unchanged: ACM table, margin, served ⇔ SINR ≥ −1.4418 dB after joint resolution, energy accounting with P_idle = 0 primary, clock/integration, geometry/10° visibility, actions, observable information, calibration λ = η_ref and κ on a nominal-greedy reference, reward core R = B − η_ref·E, Φ as QoS, C1 full-network difference surplus, C2 feature migration and forecast schema, C3 as set-level consolidation coordinator, learning contract, history seal) and §3 (known-answer suite, extended for (a) with coupled-power convergence/saturation and slot-consistent interference fixtures).
    14	- **Service definition:** PHY decodability with QoS co-primaries (astra §2 item 10, 23). A guaranteed-rate service endpoint is not declared; if the owner later requires one it is a separate, additional endpoint.
    15	
    16	## Rules that make "whichever helps C3" honest
    17	- The primary is (a) by requirement 1, not by C3's outcome. C3's marginal is measured under every cell and reported as a regime map ("where does coordination change EE"). A positive C3 under (b) with a non-positive C3 under (a) is a reported finding, not grounds to swap the primary after the fact.
    18	- Training admission (astra §4): retained factors need positive oracle marginals beyond certified numerical error and acceptable QoS; C3 additionally needs genuine joint headroom (a multi-user witness beating the unilateral alternative) and a deployable S0 gain ≥ the pre-existing 1 % practical threshold. If C3's set-level oracle marginal is ≤ 0 in every completed, physically defensible cell, C3 training/screens/confirmation close and a bounded negative is reported; C1/C2 proceed under their own gates.
    19	- No target, standby, margin, service or priority change after outcomes are opened. Any defect found later is repaired and re-run, never demoted by outcome.
    20	
    21	## Ordering
    22	1. Codex implements one versioned radiation/rate/energy engine with the three architectures behind a declared switch, the known-answer suite, and the matrix runner reusing Track B's shared-tape lever-matrix runner. Nothing runs before the KAT suite passes.
    23	2. Rehearsal to measure q; overnight matrix (≤ 160 core-hours); every cell reported.
    24	3. Stage A regenerated sources + training (FULL2, DROP_C1, DROP_C2, ALL_NEUTRAL; three initialisations) only for factors admitted by the probes; stage C ladder; C3-S screens and confirmatory on fresh worlds.
    25	4. Stage A real launch stays HOLD until step 2 admits the factors; `PHYSICS-GO.txt` names `V025-ANGLE-TPC-TDM-ACM`.
    26	
    27	Seal: this file's sha256 is recorded in `V025-PHYSICS-SUCCESSOR-PRIORITY-DECLARATION-2026-09-08.sha256`; the astra round-3 consolidation it binds is `ADJUDICATION-PHYSICS-EE-ROUND3-CONSOLIDATION-CODEX-GPT6-ASTRA-ULTRA-2026-09-08.md` (sha256 recorded in the same sidecar).

FILE controller-records/V025-PHYSICS-SUCCESSOR-PRIORITY-DECLARATION-v1.1-AMENDMENT-2026-09-08.md
     1	# V025 priority declaration — v1.1 amendment (controller, sealed before any successor outcome; 2026-09-08, server clock ≈ 14:35 UTC)
     2	
     3	v1.0 (`V025-PHYSICS-SUCCESSOR-PRIORITY-DECLARATION-2026-09-08.md`, sha256 e45f2f025a230a7d66ddd16c3b369c52979c177f58927e016228e4b3dc800020) is preserved unchanged. This amendment applies astra round 4 (`astra-physics-round4-final.md`: `PRIMARY=a-r | ADD_CELLS=a-r0,a′-r0 | R_STAR=50 Mbit/s (synthetic) | C1_LEVER_UNDER_RATE_TARGET=collapses`) and the fresh-context C3 adjudication's finding that a constant-SINR target does not create the occupancy → required-power mechanism. No successor outcome exists at sealing time.
     4	
     5	## Amendments
     6	1. **Primary architecture: (a-r) `V025-ANGLE-RATE-TPC-TDM-ACM`** — memoryless angle-aware power control with a per-user nominal rate target r* = 50 000 000 bit/s (inherited as a synthetic operating point from Track B lever L1; explicitly not calibrated demand). Equal-airtime full-band TDM. Required SINR from the frozen ACM profile: Γ_r(n_b) = min{γ_m : W·SE_m/n_b ≥ r*}; slot power p_u = min(1.65 W, Γ_r(n_b)·(N₀W + Î_u)/ĥ_u), ĥ_u = G^T(θ_u)·L_u·G^R; history-independent coupled solving; slot-integrated PA accounting. Angle drives power through ĥ_u; occupancy drives power through Γ_r(n_b).
     7	2. **Infeasibility / accounting:** if no MODCOD meets the rate at the cap, mark the target infeasible and transmit at the RF cap; keep actual partial delivery, interference and energy; no pruning or repacking. PHY service (decodability) is unchanged; rate-target attainment is reported separately. Bits = achieved decodable ACM bits (full buffer).
     8	3. **Matrix:** the original 18 cells are retained with a/a′ relabelled a-γ/a′-γ; two cells added: **a-r0** and **a′-r0** (FDM: sub-band-consistent noise/interference, summed RF, equal 1.65/n_b sub-caps). Priority order (fixed now): `a-r0 > a′-r0 > a-γ0 > b0 > a′-γ0`, then the S / H / SH / T treatments in the same architecture order; U cells diagnostic only.
     9	4. **Components under the primary:** C1 = whole-network difference surplus (its positive marginal is expected through energy and service, not surplus bits — accepted); C2 = future required-power / cap / service-survival forecasts (astra round 3 §2 items 26–28); C3 = set-level coordinator scoring whole configurations, with coordinated load transfers / swaps included alongside evacuations, one prospectively frozen catalogue across matched arms.
    10	5. **Admission (unchanged):** acceptance suite, QoS, genuine joint-headroom witness, S0 deployable gain ≥ 1 %, FULL/DROP marginals; goal 2 requires all three positive; the primary's identity cannot change with outcome signs.
    11	6. **First probe cell:** a-r0 on fresh shared TRAIN tapes with FULL, all DROP arms, unilateral / joint / deployable S0 arms and NULL / random-feasible controls. Stage A remains HOLD until admission.
    12	
