FILE controller-records/V025-CONTROLLER-DECISIONS-ACM-FIX-PROBE-SPLIT-2026-09-09.md
     1	# Controller decision — split the interaction-existence probe across the ACM correction
     2	Recorded 2026-09-09, server clock 06:10 UTC. **No probe outcome exists at recording time.** No regime has reported; the running probe was still in its calibration phase.
     3	
     4	## The fact that triggered this
     5	Stage 4h landed a confirmed correction to the ACM causality defect. Verified by file hash at 06:08 UTC, the three files carrying the defect differ between the corrected engine workspace and the two workspaces that are currently executing:
     6	
     7	| file | `mcrl-v025-codex-ws-engine` (corrected) | `mcrl-v025-probe-ws` and `mcrl-v025-pilot-ws` (pre-fix) |
     8	|---|---|---|
     9	| `physics_v025/acm.py` | `aa58aeeb83c5…` | `361b0daba0e5…` |
    10	| `physics_v025/resolution.py` | `e0b1cc50532a…` | `7fbad160d831…` |
    11	| `physics_v025/batch.py` | `3677d530f348…` | `350f86d9b9c2…` |
    12	
    13	The interaction-existence probe launched at 05:43 UTC and the stage-C pilot are therefore both executing the **pre-fix** physics.
    14	
    15	## Why this matters to the probe's question
    16	The probe asks whether, re-anchored at a certified iterated unilateral optimum `u`, any strictly improving joint move exists, that is whether `max Psi_A^u > 0`. On the stage-4h paired smoke the correction moves availability from 0.791277 to 0.453138 and pooled EE from 18,940,246 to 5,658,947 bit/J at identical joules. The corrected physics is therefore **strictly more contended**.
    17	
    18	The inference this licenses is asymmetric, and the asymmetry is the whole reason for this decision:
    19	
    20	* A **positive** result on the pre-fix physics is suggestive but is measured on physics we do not intend to publish.
    21	* A **null** result on the pre-fix physics does **not** transfer to the corrected physics. Less contention means less for a coordination layer to exploit, so a null there is exactly the result the corrected physics is least bound by.
    22	
    23	Accepting a pre-fix null as the answer to the C3 existence question would be an error of the same kind the project has already made twice: measuring the interaction term in a regime where it is structurally suppressed, then reading the suppression as an absence.
    24	
    25	## Decision
    26	1. The corrected-ACM probe is launched **in parallel**, in a new workspace `/home/sat/mcrl-v025-probe-ws-acmfix`, over the same six regimes (`a-r0`, `R1`, `R3`, `R4`, `R6`, `R7`), with the question, protocol, calibration reference, step count, seeds and search budget **unchanged**. Only `src/mcrl/physics_v025/` is swapped.
    27	2. The pre-fix probe is **allowed to finish**. It is not killed and its result is not discarded. It becomes the "before" arm of a paired pre-fix / post-fix contrast, which is itself informative: if interaction exists only after the correction, the ACM defect is the mechanism that was suppressing it.
    28	3. Neither probe's result may be used to select the other. Both were commissioned before either reported.
    29	4. The **corrected-ACM probe is the one that answers the C3 existence question** for the paper. The pre-fix probe is reporting-only and is labelled as such.
    30	
    31	## What this decision is not
    32	This is not a rerun selected by outcome. The selecting fact is a source-file hash comparison, recorded above, made before any regime reported. This declaration does not change any threshold, sign, seed, horizon, acceptance rule or scientific gate, and it does not create a new gate.
    33	
    34	## Consequence for the stage-C pilot
    35	The pilot is also on pre-fix physics. Its energy-efficiency numbers are therefore **not comparable** to any matrix run on corrected physics, and it is reporting-only under `PILOT_NOT_CLAIM` regardless of what it produces. Its remaining value is operational: it proves the stage-C path runs end to end. That value is unaffected by the physics version.

FILE controller-records/V025-CONTROLLER-DECISIONS-COMPUTE-BUDGET-2026-09-08.md
     1	# V025 — controller decisions on compute budget and thinning order (2026-09-08 ≈ 17:50 UTC; before any real-world successor outcome)
     2	
     3	Source: provider v1 report — with the Python-object tape, the 57 525-chain cross-product inventory and the unbatched runner, the measured cost is 12.63 s per anchor of provider acquisition, 4.66 s per 48-boundary catalogue row, q ≈ 0.308, ≈ 182 868 core-hours for the plan (budget: 160). This is an engineering failure of the current implementation, not a property of the physics; the decisions below fix the implementation first and only then thin the plan, in a pre-declared order.
     4	
     5	1. **Engineering targets (stage 4, before any thinning):** dense per-step numpy tapes (provider decision 9); realisable inventory only (≈ 2 760 chains, decision 4/D4); batched evaluation of a whole catalogue per anchor — the capped fixed point, ACM lookup, energy and bits computed for all configurations of an anchor in one vectorised pass over (configuration × boundary); provider acquisition amortised once per world (48 × 30 boundaries computed once and shared by all settings and arms). Target: ≤ 0.02 s per catalogue row per anchor and ≤ 1 s per anchor of provider work on the reference hardware; the rehearsal reports both.
     6	2. **Catalogue size cap (decision 4 refined):** pairwise joint moves are restricted to the top-K = 10 users by nominal unilateral surplus **and their top-2 legal options each** (≤ 45 × 4 = 180 rows); unilateral rows ≤ users × legal options (≈ 2 700); evacuation sets ≤ active beams (≈ 40); S0 proposals ≤ 200. Catalogue ≤ ≈ 3 200 rows per anchor.
     7	3. **Thinning order if the rehearsed projection still exceeds 160 core-hours** (apply the smallest step that fits; record every applied step in the seal; never chosen by outcome): (i) anchor stride k = 2, then 3 (decision item 3); (ii) treatment settings dropped from the **bottom of the sealed priority order** (T cells first, then SH, then H, then S — within each, the lowest-priority architectures first); the five architecture baselines `a-r0, a′-r0, a-γ0, b0, a′-γ0` and the U diagnostics are never dropped; (iii) probe worlds reduced from 4 to 3 only if (i)–(ii) are insufficient, and then the claim is labelled accordingly.
     8	4. **What is never thinned:** the 12 + 1 arms per setting (the arms are the science), the 48-boundary integration, the calibration procedure, the placebo and dry-run.
     9	5. **Reporting:** the rehearsal writes a cost table (per world: provider seconds; per anchor: rows, seconds; projection per setting) into the seal package; the projection and the applied thinning steps are sealed before the first unit opens.

FILE controller-records/V025-CONTROLLER-DECISIONS-CONSOLIDATE-2026-09-09.md
     1	# Controller decision — stop the broad search and cut to the minimum set
     2	Recorded 2026-09-09, server clock about 09:20 UTC. **No probe result has been read.** The reason below is a method fact, not an outcome.
     3	
     4	## Why the broad search stops
     5	The `acm2` interaction-existence probe searches a bounded neighbourhood for a configuration with positive interaction. That question now has a **predicted answer to verify instead of a space to search**:
     6	
     7	* round 11A derives the exact condition under which a beam holding one or two users selects no transmitted mode while three activate one;
     8	* the engine's own quantile was checked against it and sits inside the window at every realistic elevation, `q10 = 0.42923539` at 10 degrees against a window of `0.3483373150 <= q < 0.6237348355`.
     9	
    10	Verifying one predicted configuration costs minutes. Searching a neighbourhood for it costs hours and six concurrent processes each holding an 800 MB tape. When the prediction is this specific, the search is the wrong instrument.
    11	
    12	## The operational reason, stated plainly
    13	I oversubscribed the machine. Two probe arms each building their own tapes caused an out-of-memory stall, and the load has sat between 32 and 64 on 20 cores with repeated loss of connectivity. That is my error and it has cost hours today. Running fewer things is not caution here; it is the only way anything finishes.
    14	
    15	## What runs
    16	| job | why it stays |
    17	|---|---|
    18	| the predicted-configuration witness test | answers today's question, minutes of compute |
    19	| the adversarial margin review | decides whether the mechanism is real physics or an artefact of a defective rule |
    20	| the minimal stage-C pilot | operational proof that the training path runs end to end |
    21	
    22	## What stops
    23	| job | why it stops |
    24	|---|---|
    25	| `acm2` broad neighbourhood search | superseded by the prediction; no result read |
    26	| widened neighbourhood arm | already paused; same reason, and its families were designed around a ranking argument since withdrawn |
    27	| the deadline measurement at scale | the fix is implemented and its report's results sections are empty placeholders. The matrix is withheld tonight for other reasons, so the measurement is not on today's critical path |
