FILE controller-records/V025-CONTROLLER-DECLARATION-ULP-TOLERANCE-2026-09-10.md
     1	# Declared change — the replay parity gate is relaxed from bit-exact to 2 ULP
     2	
     3	**2026-09-10. Written BEFORE any demand-capped result exists. No sealed constant,
     4	threshold, sign, seed, horizon, price, guard, acceptance rule, artefact or manifest is
     5	changed. This changes a gate in a controller-authored diagnostic prompt, not in the science.**
     6	
     7	## What happened
     8	
     9	`MSCAP` was asked to replay 128 recorded multi-start endpoints and confirm the pooled
    10	capacity efficiency reproduced the receipts **at binary64**, stopping if it did not. That
    11	gate was written by the controller.
    12	
    13	It failed on 5 of 128 endpoints, 9 field values in all. The worker stopped as instructed and
    14	reported no capped result. **It followed the instruction correctly.**
    15	
    16	## Why the gate was wrong
    17	
    18	Every one of the nine mismatches is **exactly one unit in the last place**:
    19	
    20	| field | relative difference | ULP of the value | mismatch / ULP |
    21	|---|---:|---:|---:|
    22	| bits (w3/s1) | 1.710e-16 | 1.526e-05 | **1.00** |
    23	| ee_bit_per_j (w3/s1) | 1.880e-16 | 7.451e-09 | **1.00** |
    24	| bits (w4/s0) | 1.917e-16 | 1.526e-05 | **1.00** |
    25	| joules (w4/s0) | 1.847e-16 | 4.547e-13 | **1.00** |
    26	| joules (w1/s0) | 1.314e-16 | 4.547e-13 | **1.00** |
    27	| joules (w1/s1) | 1.325e-16 | 4.547e-13 | **1.00** |
    28	| ee_bit_per_j (w1/s1) | 1.602e-16 | 7.451e-09 | **1.00** |
    29	| joules (w3/s1) | 1.352e-16 | 4.547e-13 | **1.00** |
    30	| ee_bit_per_j (w3/s1) | 1.590e-16 | 7.451e-09 | **1.00** |
    31	
    32	Double precision epsilon is 2.220e-16. Nine out of nine at exactly 1 ULP is the signature of
    33	**summation order**, not of a physical or accounting discrepancy. Floating-point addition is
    34	not associative; a replay that pools in a different order than the recording cannot be
    35	bit-identical, and demanding that it be is a defect in the gate.
    36	
    37	This is corroborated independently: `EVALPATH-2026-09-10.md` reports that with both
    38	evaluation paths on all 48 boundaries, realised-field parity is "numerical but never fully
    39	binary64-identical in this sample."
    40	
    41	## The declared change
    42	
    43	**The replay parity gate becomes: every replayed field must agree with its receipt to within
    44	2 ULP of the receipt value, and the count of fields exceeding 1 ULP must be reported.**
    45	Any mismatch above 2 ULP still stops the job.
    46	
    47	## Why this is not tuning against an observed result
    48	
    49	- The quantity being gated is **instrument reproducibility**, not any scientific outcome.
    50	  No route's sign, no EE figure, and no acceptance rule depends on it.
    51	- **No demand-capped number has been computed.** The job stopped before producing one, so
    52	  there is no observed result to tune toward. The relaxation is declared while the outcome
    53	  is still unknown.
    54	- The new tolerance is fixed by IEEE 754, not chosen to admit the observed mismatches: 1 ULP
    55	  is the smallest representable disagreement, and the bound is set at 2 ULP before rerunning.
    56	- The rerun is **not outcome-selected**. It is a rerun of a job that produced **no** result,
    57	  for a reason established to be an artefact of the gate.
    58	
    59	## What is still owed
    60	
    61	The `EVALPATH` finding that global path authority is `UNDETERMINED` is **not** resolved by
    62	this declaration and is not affected by it. It remains on the owed-repair register.

FILE controller-records/V025-CONTROLLER-DESIGN-C3-PANEL-SPINE-2026-09-10.md
     1	# §C3 panel — the design decisions that can be fixed now, and the two that wait
     2	Recorded 2026-09-10, before the panel exists and before any source-training contrast has been measured. `DIAGNOSTIC_NOT_CLAIM`. Nothing here changes an arm definition, a source, a target, a price, a guard or an acceptance criterion; it fixes construction and reporting.
     3	
     4	## Fixed now
     5	
     6	**Arms — nine, plus the external control.** The sealed six: the full arm, three leave-one-out arms by neutral-source substitution with all heads retained and deployed, the all-neutral control, and the external geometry-only baseline. Plus the three single-informative arms the owner's requirement needs and the contract lacks. The leave-one-in contrast is half the requirement; without those arms that half cannot be evaluated.
     7	
     8	**Construction — each arm keeps its own seed and catalogue.** A measured probe found **zero** intersection between the full arm's and the first drop arm's catalogues at every anchor tested, so a shared catalogue is unsound the moment arms carry their own learned seeds. Instead a **shared physical cache** evaluates each configuration once per identical physical context, and for the one-step pooled comparison only the **union of chosen configurations** is realised — at most nine outcomes per anchor. Cached realised outcomes must never leak into selection, and cache keys bind tape, world, time, physical and run settings, evaluator identity, the nominal-versus-realised field, the boundary set and the prefix history; raw configuration identifiers are insufficient because base identifiers embed carrier names.
     9	
    10	**Local search — one for every arm, and it is first-improvement.** Accepting the first strict improvement reaches a different and better fixed point than completing a best-improvement sweep, on all twenty anchors under both provisioning rules, at 8.13 % and 1.62 % higher pooled efficiency. This is a search-order choice rather than a physics change, it was found while measuring something else, and it is better for every arm equally, so declaring it is not outcome-selection. **It must be stated in the panel's declaration, because the same neighbourhood with a different traversal order reaches a different local optimum.**
    11	
    12	**Reading — the degeneracy screen already pre-declared.** Below-reference is decided by exact sign against the head-independent certified fixed point; every contrast reports both the all-anchor marginal and the marginal over anchors where every arm in the contrast is at or above reference.
    13	
    14	**An asymmetry that must appear in the results table.** Dropping the third route changes **zero** proposed assignments at every anchor tested; dropping the first changes 12 to 26 and the second 29 to 69. The third route's ablation acts through ranking alone, the first two also move the proposal. A table that does not say so invites the reader to assume the three are mechanistically alike.
    15	
    16	**Seeds.** For a paired ordering test the learner seed is a nuisance replicate and the cluster is date by seed; with many dates most variance is across worlds. Three to five seeds are enough for the ordering on the added arms; the full seed count is reserved for the full arm and the three leave-one-out arms.
    17	
    18	## Run under both provisioning rules
    19	The provisioning decision is unresolved and is blocked on framing rather than evidence. **The panel does not have to wait for it.** The adjudication's own conditions already require publishing both rules, so running every arm under both discharges that condition and removes the dependency. It costs twice, and that is the honest price of not prejudging a decision that is not mine.
    20	
    21	Running only under the sealed rule would measure the routes on a model that credits nothing on three quarters of its transmissions. Running only under the corrected rule would enact an unauthorised change to declared physics. Both is the only option that is neither.
    22	
    23	## What waits, and on what
    24	- **Row-building path.** Whether rows are built through the exact path or the surrogate is being costed now. The surrogate writes geometric legality into both the validity and survival fields and is wrong on 822 of 1,784 rows; a cheaper option that changes a label is not acceptable at any price.
    25	- **Anchor and date allocation.** Waits on the same cost measurement.
    26	
    27	## Standing
    28	No panel is authorised by this note and no run is started. It exists so that the construction is fixed before any number exists, and so that a later reader can see which choices preceded the results.

