    94	## H4 — degeneracy report
    95	
    96	`degeneracy_report` is reporting-only. It never filters its input anchors. It requires reference metadata declaring a head-independent fixed-point certificate and rejects malformed certificate identities. Below-reference status uses exact cross multiplication:
    97	
    98	```text
    99	arm_bits × reference_joules < reference_bits × arm_joules
   100	```
   101	
   102	There is no epsilon, tolerance, or threshold. Floats are converted to their exact binary64 rational values before comparison.
   103	
   104	For every named pairwise contrast, the report returns both:
   105	
   106	1. the ratio-of-sums pooled-EE marginal on all input anchors; and
   107	2. the same marginal on the supplementary subset where both arms are at or above reference.
   108	
   109	The all-anchor rows remain present. An empty restricted subset reports no marginal rather than altering the population.
   110	
   111	Each arm also reports its below-reference count, fraction, and the ordered per-anchor positive shortfall distribution in bits/J (plus minimum and maximum). These are supplementary diagnostics; they do not gate or remove an anchor.
   112	
   113	The smoke reports SEALED and MARGIN_Q separately. However, its certificate is only a hash over the bounded smoke BASELINE neighbourhood and a head-independent score ordering. It does not invoke the pre-declared controller's authoritative full-neighbourhood certified reference builder. The certificate is therefore self-attested, and H4 remains incomplete despite the reporting arithmetic being correct.
