/home/sat/mcrl-v025-c1c2-ws/V025-STAGES-6-8-CONTRACT-v1.2-AMENDMENT-2026-09-09.md:5:1. **§B5 corrected — interaction labels are uncapped.** Ψ_A for a selected coalition costs |A| + 2 evaluations, so it is computed for every coalition regardless of size (v1.7 erratum item 3). Only the exact per-user Shapley attribution remains capped at |A| ≤ 4 and is reporting-only. C3 training rows therefore carry Ψ_A for the actual selected set, with `credit_split = NOT_COMPUTED_LARGE_SET` above the cap.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-c1c2-ws/V025-STAGES-6-8-CONTRACT-v1.2-AMENDMENT-2026-09-09.md:6:2. **§C2 — feature sufficiency for the set-conditioned head.** The encoder's input must contain, for the changed-user set and its affected beams: proposed and incumbent associations by physical identity, background occupancy and activation before and after insertion, the shared-resource relations among the affected beams, and the **pairwise cross-gain terms among the affected beams** (not only a scalar interference summary — a summary can hide exactly the difference that flips a coupled fixed point). Acceptance test T2 is extended: the information-twin pair must be separable with the full context and provably ambiguous when the cross-gain block is removed.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-c1c2-ws/V025-STAGES-6-8-CONTRACT-v1.2-AMENDMENT-2026-09-09.md:7:3. **§C4 / report schema — honest axes for a learned S3.** Over one catalogue that is exactly evaluated, S3 cannot exceed S0's maximum of the same score; therefore the only admissible learned claims are (i) better realised closed-loop pooled EE under model mismatch, (ii) equal decision quality at materially lower measured end-to-end computation, or (iii) a measured residual task (search allocation, evaluation-count reduction). The claim axis is named before training. A learned escape proposer over a wider neighbourhood is **not** part of this study; it may be proposed later with its own declaration and only if profiling shows evaluation is the bottleneck.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-c1c2-ws/V025-STAGES-6-8-CONTRACT-v1.2-AMENDMENT-2026-09-09.md:9:5. **Report schema — anti-pattern statistics (round 9D).** The terminal report must contain, per contrast: net collision-avoidance value with both components unclipped; the additive-reversal frequency and whether the coordinator prevents them; escape recall and harmful-acceptance rate stratified by coalition size; top-choice agreement between the learned and exact selectors; the full decision-latency distribution including feature construction, catalogue generation, physics-call count, timeout frequency and fallback-inclusive outcomes; and the four experiments of §C3 reported separately and never interchanged.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-selector-ws/C1-RESOURCE-CONTEXT-2026-09-10.md:17:A coalition-wide vector depends on the other proposed member actions, while the C1 interface is action-local (`deployment.py:626-645`). I therefore did not feed those stored values to C1. For every exact singleton receipt I rebuilt the same 163 coordinate formulas from the reference profile and that focal `(user, action)` alone. No coordinate family was excluded: all 28 affected-beam pool values, 129 pairwise-cross-gain values, and six globals pass the pre-decision/no-fixed-point rule in this singleton form. Only 28 of the 163 slots vary on held-out singleton actions; coalition-induced variation in the other slots is unavailable under the focal-action-only rule. The candidate outcome, label, power fixed point, and whole-network result are absent from feature construction.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-selector-ws/C1-RESOURCE-CONTEXT-2026-09-10.md:21:The harness uses 10253 exact coalition fitting rows and 33670 unique singleton actions across the frozen split. It reuses seed `20260910`, the three-anchor-block split, the fixed-ReLU random-feature ridge family with raw linear skip, and the exact six-point grid from the parametrisation comparison. Each shared per-user scorer is fitted through the sum of its member differences on the original coalition rows. Exact singleton targets are read from Fraction receipts; the pilot fallback is never read as a target. Re-evaluated defining terms reconstruct those receipts with maximum residual 1.030e-13 on development and 7.749e-14 on test.
