/home/sat/mcrl-v025-c1c2-ws/V025-PILOT-MIN-REPORT-2026-09-09.md:85:The C2 tie-break diagnostic is the fraction of non-incumbent (user, action) candidates whose C2 head score is exactly equal to the incumbent's under the FULL arm, i.e. C2 cannot discriminate the move and the ranking falls through to C1 plus the stable configuration-ID tie-break. `c2_tie_frequency` is the fraction of anchor-seed decisions with any such tie; `c2_tie_pair_fraction_mean` is the mean per-decision tie fraction. See DEFECTS.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-c1c2-ws/V025-PILOT-MIN-REPORT-2026-09-09.md:110:- **D-MIN-2 (suspicious result, unexplained). `S_UNI` is exactly degenerate with `BASELINE`.** Pooled EE for `S_UNI` equals `BASELINE` to the last digit (16 987 632 bits/J) at every one of the 5 anchors. Under the 5 s pilot `compute_budget_s`, `_s_uni_select` returned the carrier base unchanged, i.e. it found no accepted unilateral improvement at all. The `FULL-vs-S_UNI` contrast below is therefore **not** a comparison against exhaustive unilateral improvement; per contract v1.2 item 6 it is at best a budget-limited operational comparator, and in this run it is an empty one. Do not read it as evidence.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-c1c2-ws/V025-PILOT-MIN-REPORT-2026-09-09.md:111:- **D-MIN-3 (suspicious result). `FULL` selects the all-users coalition (size 100) at every anchor-seed.** `escape_and_harm_by_coalition_size` shows `selected: 10` at size 100 and `selected: 0` at every size 2-6, while positive-joint escape opportunities exist at sizes 2-6. A selector that always moves all 100 users is far more likely to be an artefact of the epoch-200 head's scale than a real decision. Two of those ten selections were harmful by exact joint delta (harmful-acceptance rate 0.2).
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-c1c2-ws/V025-PILOT-MIN-REPORT-2026-09-09.md:113:- **D-MIN-5 (now measured, previously zero-by-construction). C2 tie frequency.** The build-3 code had no C2 tie-break and the field was hard-coded `False`. This pilot implemented the smallest schema-satisfying measurement: the fraction of non-incumbent (user, action) candidates whose FULL-arm C2 head score exactly equals the incumbent's. Measured value: **0.0** on both catalogue anchors (`c2_tie_frequency` 0.0, `c2_tie_pair_fraction_mean` 0.0). The C2 head discriminates every candidate; the zero is now an observation rather than an artefact, but it is still a proxy for head indiscriminability, not for a build-3 tie-break code path.
