/home/sat/mcrl-v025-probe-ws/EVALPATH-2026-09-10.md:100:The cited pilot script is absent from this copy. For source audit only, I read `/home/sat/mcrl-v025-selector-ws/scripts/run_v025_pilot_c3.py`; its engine copy SHA-256 exactly matches the workspace engine (`d430baf38eee7973aa56a503e905548bbf55ae4a5eb6f2435c2a2543d4786196`). The pilot script also byte-matches `/home/sat/mcrl-v025-pilot-ws/scripts/run_v025_pilot_c3.py` (`95103bb96caaa130659fa0d509f19409574b406798a173e278a7d9dac12b7435`). No sibling file was modified.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-probe-ws/EVALPATH-2026-09-10.md:105:- **Pilot evaluation’s exact boundary-0 selectors are mixed.** `_exact_s0_boundary0` batch-populates candidates but retains scalar BASE, then ranks raw bits (`:1458-1500`). The call into `_s_uni_select` reuses that evaluator (`:1638-1652`); `_s_uni_select` reads BASE/current with `evaluate` and batches candidate neighborhoods (`run_v025_matrix_probe.py:1831-1924`), so its first sweep compares scalar BASE with dense candidates. `_exact_interactions` similarly batches catalogues/singletons and subtracts its cached anchor (`run_v025_pilot_c3.py:1328-1379`); P-a0 uses scalar BASE as that anchor. These can alter S0/S_UNI selection, joint deltas, and ψ—not merely reporting.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-probe-ws/EVALPATH-2026-09-10.md:106:- At the eight sampled real BASE anchors, the dense-minus-scalar bit gap was −13.2449 to +21.2834 κ. Including the pilot’s η-priced energy term, the exact constant error injected into a dense-candidate minus scalar-BASE objective ranged from −17.2608 to +28.6520 κ. This is the appropriate rough corruption scale for mixed source/selection differences. It is not an EE percentage.
